{
    "background_story": "Raphael was a brilliant and reclusive scholar who spent most of his life studying the ancient Indian texts of the Vedanga. A Sanskrit expert, he was particularly fascinated by the Jyotish Vedanga, the ancient Indian astronomy and astrology. Raphael's obsession with the Vedanga led him to spend years deciphering the intricate relationships between the celestial bodies and their influence on human affairs. His groundbreaking research earned him recognition in academic circles, but Raphael remained humble and dedicated to his craft. He believed that the Vedanga held the secrets of the universe, and he spent his life unraveling its mysteries. Raphael's work became a testament to the enduring power of ancient wisdom and the human quest for knowledge.",
